This file is the notice; the full texts are in the two files beside it and both
apply to this work.

  MIT Licence          see LICENSE-MIT
  Apache Licence 2.0   see LICENSE-APACHE

Why dual rather than MIT alone: Apache-2.0 contributes an express patent grant
and a patent-retaliation clause, which a cryptographic and networking core
should carry. It is also the licence every dependency in this workspace already
offers (rustls is Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT, chacha20 and cipher are MIT OR
Apache-2.0), so the dual grant introduces no friction for
a downstream packager.

Why not MPL-2.0, which this project previously carried: MPL-2.0 is file-level
copyleft, and its only advantage here was matching Xray-core's licence to keep
a future code-sharing door open. That door is better kept open by running
upstream's test suites against this implementation in CI than by holding a
copyleft licence in reserve.

Upstream implementations are not vendored into this repository. Xray-core
(MPL-2.0), sing-box (GPL-3.0) and AmneziaWG (MIT) are compared against by
executing their suites, not by copying their code or their tests, so none of
their terms attach to this work.

